{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>However, any ḥerem</b> etc. Rashi explained: some say that unspecified ḥerem-dedications are for sacred property, for the upkeep of the Temple, as Rashi explained below, to Elazar — from any ḥerem it is קדש קדשים." "<b>It shall not be sold and shall not be redeemed.</b> Rashi explained: according to the one who says etc., he interprets this verse with reference to unspecified ḥerem-dedications, and this is what the verse says: 'however, any ḥerem,' that is, any unspecified ḥerem — it shall not be sold and shall not be redeemed, but shall be given to the priests. And according to the one who says that unspecified ḥerem-dedications are for the upkeep of the Temple, he interprets this verse with reference to priestly ḥerem-dedications, and this is what the verse says: 'however, any ḥerem,' that is, when one says: 'the value of this animal — it is upon me as a ḥerem to the priest' — concerning this the verse says: it shall not be sold and shall not be redeemed, for all agree etc.; but in the case of unspecified ḥerem-dedications, that is, divine ḥerem, they are redeemed." "<b>Any ḥerem is קדש קדשים.</b> Rashi explained: to teach that priestly ḥerem-dedications take effect etc. That is, if one priest says about קדשי קדשים or about ordinary sacrifices of his own: 'they are upon me as a ḥerem to the priest — the value of these sacrifices,' the ḥerem takes effect upon them, and he gives the valuation money to another priest, as Rashi explained: if it was a נדר etc.; but if one dedicates his fellow's sacrifices by ḥerem, by reasoning he gives the money, whether they are a נדר or a נדבה, as is derived in the chapter 'One who dedicates his field': a person may dedicate by ḥerem his sacrifices, whether קדשי קדשים or ordinary sacrifices — if a נדר, he gives their value, and if a נדבה, he gives its enhancement value. How so? 'This ox is an עלה' — they assess how much a person wishes to give for this ox to offer it as an עלה, even though he is not obligated."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:16:03.783505571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}